INT. TRAMPOLINE PARK AFTER HOURS - NIGHT

Wall-to-wall black mesh under strings of blue neon. A foam pit like a cloud. Four teenagers in socks, breathing hard from the climb, perch on the edge of the highest platform.

PRIYA SANDOVAL-KHAN, sixteen, the ringleader. NOAH BRENNAN, seventeen, her ex. MARISELA TORRES, sixteen, her best friend. And JASPER "JAZZ" ODUYA, fifteen, the youngest, holding a phone like a torch.

PRIYA
On three, we jump.

NOAH
You said that at two.

MARISELA
She said it at one.

JAZZ
Can I film it?

PRIYA
No.

NOAH
Yes.

PRIYA
Noah, if you film me --

NOAH
What, Priya? What?

MARISELA
Guys --

PRIYA
Don't "guys" me.

JAZZ
I'm going to jump now.

NOAH
Jazz, don't --

He jumps. The rest scramble after him, shouting, a tangle of limbs. Priya and Noah collide mid-air, bounce apart, land on opposite trampolines. Marisela belly-flops into the pit and surfaces coughing foam. Jazz lies spread-eagled on the mesh, laughing. Everyone stops. Everyone stares at each other. The neon hums.

MARISELA
(from the pit)
I think I broke something.

PRIYA
(softly)
Me too.
